Also existing test 'swipes and Continues through all four pages' pumps without a registry — gate inactive, swipe works. Good.

But wait: with physics change applied only when `gated` (page==1 && gate active), in the first test... registry is null, so fine.

One more consideration: while on page 1 gated, user could tap... no other way past. Also initialPage: 2 or 3 with gate active? Initial page beyond gate — should we allow swiping back? If a user is dropped at page 3 with gate active (not possible in app since flow starts at 0, but initialPage param exists). Our physics only disables when _page == 1. If on page 2 gated (initialPage: 2), swipe back would be allowed — swipe from 2 to 1 is backward (offset > 0) — allowed; forward from 2 to 3 would be allowed by our logic, though the user reached 2 illegitimately. To be safe, maybe block forward swiping whenever gate active regardless of page:

